- op: discuss  # f85d
  at: '2026-08-20T22:24:40Z'  # f85d
  by: agent  # f85d
  actor: jgstern_agent  # f85d
  clock: 5  # f85d
  nonce: f85d  # f85d
  message: "FIX DESIGN, with a trap found by reading the control rather than assuming it. THE LAZY FIX IS WRONG. 'Derive TAINT_CALL_EDGE_TYPES from the registry' sounds right and would be a REGRESSION: the four sets that look like they name the call family do not name the same concept. TAINT_CALL_EDGE_TYPES = {calls, module_attr_ref, dispatches_to} contains module_attr_ref for WI-lokuv (attribute-read edges for io_primitives declared under attributes:, e.g. os.environ / sys.argv -- without it, auto-imported TaintSource records for attribute-kind primitives never match in structural propagation) and dispatches_to for framework-dispatch visibility. Neither is a call-family member in the call_construct sense. Replacing the set wholesale with call_family_edge_types() would DELETE both and silently break attribute-kind taint sources. THE SHAPE THAT IS CORRECT: derive only the half that IS the call family and keep the taint-specific additions explicit with their existing rationale comments intact -- TAINT_CALL_EDGE_TYPES = call_family_edge_types() | frozenset({module_attr_ref, dispatches_to}). Add a resolver call_family_edge_types() to axis_meta_keys mirroring the existing access_mode_applicable_edge_types() accessor, reading call_construct's applicable_edge_types (declared by WI-toruz at 4ff442c5b0). That makes the registry the single source for the call-family half while leaving the two taint-specific extras as declared, commented additions. verify_claims._CALL_SITE_EDGE_TYPES is already exactly call_family | {module_attr_ref}, so it can adopt the same resolver and stop agreeing with the registry by coincidence. LEAVING ALONE, deliberately: _STARVATION_CALL_EDGE_TYPES = {calls}. It is narrow ON PURPOSE and carries its own rationale (an unused import must not read as analyzer blindness); widening it is a separate decision with its own evidence, not a free rider on this fix. SECOND-ORDER RISK TO MEASURE, not to assume away: adding an edge type to the taint walk ADDS edges, and LIVE.md records that INV-foluz MANUFACTURES SUPPRESSION -- more edges can let a barrier False earn a 'sanitized' verdict. So the acceptance evidence must include not just the A/B arm flipping to violated, but a check that previously-violated flows did not silently become sanitized."  # f85d
