- op: discuss  # 1103
  at: '2026-08-21T03:07:49Z'  # 1103
  by: agent  # 1103
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 1103
  clock: 9  # 1103
  nonce: '1103'  # 1103
  message: "VALIDATED, and the verdict is split -- recall claim CONFIRMED, precision cost MEASURED AND BAD. Tag awaits_bakeoff_validation stripped per the tagging-discipline lifecycle (the metric moved; it moved partly the wrong way, which is filed rather than folded into this closure).\n\nDESIGN. Not a re-run of measurement 0001, which could not have answered this: 0001 census population was 60 flows on 2026-08-11 and the SAME five repos produce 298 at this fix parent commit nine days later, so a straight re-run would have pooled 238 flows of other drift into this items account. Instead a DELTA CENSUS: baseline 148fae52b3 in an ephemeral clone, subject d8d415dd0d, the SAME instrument from the working tree in both arms, and isolated XDG_CACHE_HOME per arm so neither arm could read the others cached behavior map. Control verified BEFORE reading any number -- under the baseline path the interpreter resolves taint.py to the clone and reports {calls, dispatches_to, module_attr_ref}, unshadowed it reports that plus instantiates.\n\nRESULT. 35 flows added across all six repos, ZERO removed (so no recall cost), all 35 adjudicated, none unadjudicable. 1 TRUE POSITIVE, 34 FALSE. Marginal precision 2.9% against the ~41% band. Per-repo added: caddy 0, mitmproxy 7, poetry 4, express 0, apollo-server 0, pretix 24.\n\nTHE TRUE POSITIVE IS THIS ITEMS OWN THESIS, CONFIRMED ON A SECOND SINK. mitmproxy onboardingapp/__init__.py:39 binds os.path.expanduser to p; :42 passes p to write_magisk_module; utils/magisk.py:100 is ZipFile(path, \"w\"). The source value IS the sink call first argument, and the flow was invisible before this fix for exactly the Popen reason -- PascalCase sink, therefore an instantiates edge. So the defect this item names is real, was really hidden, and is really fixed.\n\nTHE 34 FALSE POSITIVES ARE ONE DOMINANT MECHANISM. 24 of them land on 10 distinct call sites and EVERY one is a constructor called with no arguments at all, a keyword literal, a generated temp path, or the temp-file object -- TemporaryDirectory(), TemporaryFile(), NamedTemporaryFile(delete=True), ZipFile(os.path.join(d,\"tmp.zip\")). Checked exhaustively across every constructor call site in all five pretix files, not only the reported ones. 6 more are one unanchored FILE node in mitmproxy multiplied by the sink catalogue (3 sources x 2 sinks). 4 are poetry co-location.\n\nNOT A NEW DEFECT. co-location-function and content-not-argument were already 29 of 0001 57 false positives. This fix fed a large new class of sinks into an existing documented weakness. Filed as INV-fubag (P1): a sink call taking NO arguments cannot carry taint by argument and its receiver is a module -- that is a proof, not a heuristic, and it disposes of 24 of the 34 with zero recall cost. INV-fubag carries the explicit warning that a fix must PRESERVE the mitmproxy true positive, since removing both would look like success on FP count alone.\n\nWritten up as docs/measurements/0003. Honest limit recorded there: single adjudication pass by the author of the change, where 0001 used blind second passes."  # 1103
